<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Exploring My Community – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 2nd Grade (CEFR: Pre-A1.4)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Exploring My Community</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> It's the Park!</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Introduce themselves or family members using basic personal information. Interactive: Take part in role-plays that mimic familiar everyday interactions.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can introduce themselves and family members while sharing personal information about community places (e.g., "I'm Ana, and this is the park where I play." or "My dad works at the library."). Can take part in role-plays that mimic familiar everyday interactions about community places (e.g., "Where is the park?" "It's next to the library."). Can participate in role plays about common activities with family members (e.g., Mom says, "Let's take a walk." The child says, "Yes, let's go!").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="background-color: #e0e0e0;">
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 34%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> "Community Charades" (5 min)</p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher shows flashcards of community places (park, market, school, library, church, store) and mimes an activity associated with each.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students guess the place by shouting its name. (e.g., Teacher mimes reading, students say "library!")</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher then asks simple questions: "Do you like the park?" Students respond "Yes!" or "No."</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> "Meet My Family at the Park!" (5 min)</p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher uses a puppet or pictures of "family members" (e.g., "Mom," "Dad," "Sister") and a large picture of a park.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher models introducing: "Hello! I'm Miss Ana. This is my mom. She is at the park. We play at the park. The park is big and clean."</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher focuses on clear pronunciation of /p/ in "park" and /m/ in "mom."</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher models asking for location: "Excuse me, where is the library?" and answering: "It's next to the school."</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> (2 min)</p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher points to the park picture: "Is this a park or a market?" (Expected: "A park!")</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher points to "Mom" puppet: "Is this my sister or my mom?" (Expected: "Your mom!")</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 12 min]</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Exploring My Community")</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Short illustrated dialogue on a large chart paper or projected on a screen. The dialogue features two children and their parents at the park.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Dialogue Example:</b></p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ana: "Hello! I'm Ana. This is my dad."</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Dad: "Hello!"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Tom: "Hi, Ana! I'm Tom. This is my mom. We are at the park!"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Mom: "Yes, it's a big park. Let's play!"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ana: "Where is the playground?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Tom: "It's near the big tree. Let's go!"</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Engaging in basic social interactions to introduce self and family, and ask/answer questions about familiar community places and activities.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> "Point and Say" (3 min)</p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher reads the dialogue clearly, pointing to characters and places in the illustration.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher asks: "Who is Ana? Point to Ana!" (Students point). "Where is the park? Point to the park!" (Students point).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher asks: "What do they say about the park?" (Expected: "It's a big park!")</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 8 min]</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Speaking)</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> WH-questions ("Where is it?"), Present simple ("It's the market.", "I play there."), Adjectives + nouns ("big park," "clean library"), and vocabulary (park, market, school, library, church, store, playground, next to, near).</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice: "Sentence Builder" (5 min)</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher provides sentence frames on the board with blanks. Students complete them orally, choosing from flashcards or words given by the teacher.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"This is the ___." (park/market/school). Students point and say.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"It's a ___ ___." (big park / small store / busy market). Teacher shows picture, students say.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher prompts choral repetition: "I'm Ana. This is my dad." "It's the park. We play there."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Focus on initial sounds /p/ in park, /m/ in market.</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice: "Question and Answer Chain" (5 min)</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher holds up a flashcard of a community place (e.g., "library").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher models: "Where is the library?" Students chorally respond: "It's next to the school." (using a classroom map or pre-arranged flashcards).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students in a row ask the next student: "Where is the market?" The next student answers using the preposition: "It's near the park."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Emphasize polite expressions: "Excuse me, where is the market?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction: "Family Introductions" (5 min)</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students work in pairs. Each student has 2-3 small pictures of "family members" (Mom, Dad, Sister, Brother) and a picture of one community place (park, store, home).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student A introduces: "Hi! I'm [Student A's Name]. This is my [Mom]. My [Mom] is at the [store]."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student B responds: "Hello! My name is [Student B's Name]. I play at the park."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students then switch roles and repeat. Teacher circulates, providing support and correction.</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 15 min]</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Exploring My Community")</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> "Our Community Role-Play" in small groups (3-4 students).</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b> (10 min)</p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students are divided into small groups. Each group receives a small "community map" (drawn by the teacher or students in previous lessons) with a few key places (park, school, market, library). They also receive character cards (e.g., Mom, Dad, Child 1, Child 2) and activity cards (e.g., "play," "read," "shop," "walk").</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group prepares a short role-play (3-4 sentences per student) focusing on introducing family members, describing community places, and asking/answering location questions.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Role-play Example:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Child 1: "Hi! I'm Alex. This is my mom. We are at the park!"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Mom: "Yes, it's a clean park. Let's walk!"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Child 2: "Excuse me, where is the library?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Child 1: "It's next to the school."</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Groups take turns performing their role-plays for the class or simultaneously in different corners of the classroom.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher observes and encourages, focusing on fluent communication and completion of the task rather than perfect grammar.</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 10 min]</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist and Peer Assessment.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students perform their "Our Community Role-Play" (from Stage 4).</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist):</b></p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Introduces self/family members (e.g., "I'm Ana. This is my dad.").</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses target vocabulary for community places (park, library, school).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Asks "Where is...?" and answers "It's next to..." or "It's near..."</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Pronounces /p/, /m/, /ʈʃ/ (church) intelligibly.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Participates collaboratively in the role-play.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses polite expressions (e.g., "Excuse me," "Thank you").</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> (2 min)</p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">On a small paper, students draw a happy face if "I can introduce my family" and a star if "I can say where the park is."</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They can also complete the sentence: "Today I can say: '____ is the ____'."</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 8 min]</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection Prompt:</b> (2 min)</p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new words did you use today?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was your favorite part of the role-play?"</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
            <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What aspects of the speaking activities worked well? (e.g., "Students were enthusiastic about the role-play and used 'next to' effectively.")</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson? (e.g., "Some students still struggled with 'where is it?' so I need to reinforce WH-questions. Provide more visual cues for prepositions.")</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">This speaking lesson prepares students for Lesson 4 (Writing Composition), where they will use the same vocabulary and sentence structures ("I'm ___. This is my ___. We are at the ___.") to write simple sentences and short descriptions about their community and family members.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 5 min]</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>